course: dictionary
lesson: 12595
title: Discernible: able to be noticed
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Discernible means able to be seen, heard, noticed or understood, even if only just. It is a formal word, so you will meet it in science and in serious reading.
explain: Look at the clues in this sentence: «There was no discernible difference between the two samples.» Scientists tested the samples carefully. No discernible difference means nobody could notice any difference at all.
explain: Words like this often need effort to notice. «The lamp gave off a barely discernible glow in the fog.» Barely tells you the glow was faint, but you could still notice it if you looked closely. To check your meaning, swap in «able to be noticed» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Discernible means able to be seen, heard, noticed or understood, even if only just.
fact: «Barely discernible» means so faint that you could only just notice it.
fact: «No discernible difference» means nobody could notice any change.
fact: Discernible is a formal word, so it is common in science and in serious reading.
exercise: «There was no discernible difference between the two samples.» What does discernible mean here? | Broken into pieces | Hard to pronounce | *Able to be noticed | Very large
exercise: «The lamp gave off a barely discernible glow in the fog.» What does barely discernible suggest? | *So faint it could only just be noticed | Moving quickly | Bright enough to light the whole street | Coloured bright red
exercise: «The shape was discernible through the thick fog.» Find and copy the word that means able to be seen. | thick | through | *discernible | fog
test: «Her voice was discernible above the noise of the crowd.» What does discernible mean here? | Made of wood | Silent and still | Loud and angry | *Able to be heard
test: Ms Lee asks, «Is there any discernible change in the plant?» What is she asking? | Whether the plant is green | *Whether anything can be noticed | Whether the plant is tall | Whether the plant has died
exam: «After an hour of rain, the river rose by a discernible amount.» Which meaning fits best? | Frozen solid | Too small to measure ever | *Large enough to be noticed | Coloured blue
